    a: "Fair question — 'wary of weird names… who makes this really?' is word-for-word how buyers on the deal forums put it. Here's the honest answer: it's a direct-to-consumer brand, the same road Anker's Soundcore took before everyone trusted it. What separates a real challenger from rebadged junk is whether the maker publishes specifics and stands behind them. Walla Sound puts its driver split (15W woofer + 5W tweeter), its IP67 certification and its Bluetooth 6.0 spec on the box — and backs it with a 90-day full-refund-or-replacement guarantee. Generics print a wattage number and vanish. You get three months to disagree at no cost.",
